{"ts":"2026-07-07T14:10:48.489Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Found in review #15 follow-up: pm update --body-file - fails with ENOENT (tries to open a file literally named '-'), while pm notes --add - reads stdin. Agents composing bodies from heredocs/pipes (the grep/jq/heredoc composability principle) hit this asymmetry and fall back to temp files. Inventory every --*-file flag via pm contracts, route them through a shared read-file-or-stdin helper, and record the convention in the scripting contract. Related-not-duplicate: pm-kipd (GH-438 full-item JSON on stdin), pm-a2h3 (notes/learnings --stdin parity)."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-07T14:10:48.489Z"}],"before_hash":"0415d26f657eb5a532029cd0deb3f8c5d6b97a464c19deef4c2f10db07c028fa","after_hash":"039fe2c2dd9ce33d61b888a6ba29aad607eaeb2a39edb05d62b43e0c61497136"}
{"ts":"2026-07-15T19:27:03.514Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-15T19:27:03.514Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-15T19:27:03.514Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Dogfood confirmation 2026-07-15 (review pass #89): pm create --body-file - fails ENOENT body_file_unreadable (tries to open a file literally named \"-\"), forcing a scratch-file workaround mid-review. The error's own next_steps suggest \"ls -l \\\"-\\\"\" — the recovery bundle does not know stdin is the intent. This is exactly the convention gap this item owns; --body-file should be first on the flag list when implementing."}]}],"before_hash":"039fe2c2dd9ce33d61b888a6ba29aad607eaeb2a39edb05d62b43e0c61497136","after_hash":"58f9d428c1cf37fd9e40c816512189667392e0b7ca5f19068634974d9faeabc5"}
